# Evidence: move-bus packed words (bridge gap 1 closed)

Task: extend `code/tests/lean/Metronome/Bridge/Core.lean` with the §6 move-bus packed
words (`mv_en`/`mv_src`/`mv_dst`/`mv_data`) and prove the cut's bus is the machine's
move list slot by slot.

Environment: Windows, Lean 4.35.0 (`leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0`, toolchain pinned in
`code/tests/lean/lean-toolchain`), core libraries only (no Mathlib, no `import Mathlib`).
`lakefile.toml` sets `moreLeanArgs = ["-DwarningAsError=true"]`, so `lake build` fails on
any warning; the build below is warning-free.

Files touched: `code/tests/lean/Metronome/Bridge/Core.lean` (extended, all 94 existing
theorems unchanged), `code/tests/lean/BRIDGE_CORE_NOTES.md` (gap 1 closed).  Neither
`Metronome/Core.lean` nor `Metronome/Machine/*.lean` was edited (`src/` untouched):
`git diff --quiet HEAD -- src` exit 0.

New theorems (33): `range3`, `coreComb_moves`, `coreComb_moves_of_xa`,
`coreComb_moves_of_idle`, `i_g_slot`, `i_s_slot`, `i_d_slot`,
`mvEnAt_bridge`, `moveCand_isSome`, `moveVal_idx`, `moveVal_src`, `moveVal_dst`,
`moveVal_v`, `moveCand_eq_some`, `moveCand_map_src`, `moveCand_map_dst`,
`moveCand_map_v`, `moveAt_eq_cand`, `any_eq_find?_isSome`, `bitOf_boolMask3`,
`mvEn_bit`, `mvEnOf_bit`, `decide_and_if`, `decide_and_not_decide_and_if`,
`not_decide_and_if`, `pack3_slice0`, `pack3_slice1`, `pack3_slice2`, `mvSrc_field`,
`mvDst_field`, `mvData_field`, `srcByte_index`, `moves_bridge`.
New definitions (7): `slotGuard`, `slotSrc`, `slotDst`, `moveEn`, `moveVal`, `moveCand`,
`pack3`.

